# Keep the working copy byte-identical to what CI checks out. core.autocrlf gives a Windows working
# copy CRLF while the Linux runner checks out LF, so Prettier, which reads the working copy, fails
# locally on files that pass in CI, and any tool that rewrites a file with LF shows every line of it
# as changed. Pinning the ending here makes every clone agree, whatever its settings.
* text=auto eol=lf
